/// 'continue' begins a loop's next iteration.
///
/// There is no such statement today: 'continue' scans as an identifier, so the
/// program fails with 'Undefined variable ''continue''.'
///
/// ⚠️ The compiler's own source works around its absence in THREE places, each
/// saying so in a comment -- Interpreter.a24 wrapping a loop body in an 'if'
/// 'because the language has no ''continue''', Parser.a24 using a nested while
/// for the same reason, CEmitter.a24 guarding a branch because 'an ''Exit''
/// here would abandon the whole of CollectUnits'.  A feature its own
/// implementers have needed three times is not speculative.
///
/// Adding it costs no existing source: 'continue' and 'goto' appear nowhere in
/// compiler/, tests/ or bench/ except inside those comments, so making them
/// keywords collides with nothing.
///
/// Fails with: Undefined variable 'continue'.
///
test 'continue begins the next iteration';
begin
    var Seen : String := '';

    for var I := 0; I < 4; I := I + 1 do
    begin
        if I = 1 then continue;
        Seen := Seen + Str (I);
    end

    AssertEqual (Str ('023'), Seen);
end
